      "content": "Yes, $73 - 46 = 27$.\n\n**Final Answer:** $\\text{IQR} = 27$\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Formula:** $\\text{IQR} = Q_3 - Q_1$\n* **What the letters mean:**\n  * $Q_3$: The upper quartile (the median of the upper half of the ordered data)\n  * $Q_1$: The lower quartile (the median of the lower half of the ordered data)\n* **Why we use it:** The interquartile range measures the spread of the middle $50\\%$ of the data, which ignores extreme high or low values (outliers) at the ends.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always write down the formula $\\text{IQR} = Q_3 - Q_1$ and show the substitution $73 - 46$ before writing the final answer. Even if you make a small arithmetic slip, showing the correct substitution can still protect your method marks."
